@startuml direct-rialto-data-flow-gating
title direct-rialto: when may playback start, and when may a sample be injected?

package "Question 1: may play() be issued?\n(AampRialtoPlaybackController)" {
  rectangle "Play request\n(AAMP called Stream() /\nRequestPlay())" as REQ
  rectangle "Holds (bit set)\nSourcesNotAttached\nFlushing\nPositionPending\nFragmentCaching\nPreRollIncomplete" as HOLDS
  rectangle "Play action fires once when\nrequest outstanding AND no hold set\n-> AampRialtoPlayer::IssuePlay()" as FIRE
  REQ --> FIRE
  HOLDS --> FIRE : all must be clear
}

package "Question 2: may a sample reach Rialto?\n(AampRialtoMediaSource, one per track)" {
  rectangle "GateMode\nNONE: flows\nBLOCKED: injector thread waits\nDROPPED: sample discarded at once" as GATE
  rectangle "Generation token\ncaptured by the injector before it blocks;\nbumped by unblockInjection()\n(Flush / Stop): an older sample is abandoned" as GEN
  rectangle "Rialto needData request\nsample is added only after Rialto asks" as ND
  GATE --> ND : passed
  GEN --> ND : still current
}

package "Question 3: is the player in a state that accepts it?\n(PlayerStateMachine)" {
  rectangle "FLUSHING: a flush owns the pipeline;\nStop()/Configure()/Flush() wait for it" as ST
}

package "Question 4: whose position is it?\n(deferred flush election)" {
  rectangle "PositionPending hold\nset by Configure()/Discontinuity();\nthe first sample of the elected track\n(video if attached, else audio)\ncalls MaybeFlushForPendingPosition()" as ELECT
  rectangle "ClaimDeferredFlush(): exactly one\ninjector thread runs Flush(position)\nthen Stream()" as CLAIM
  ELECT --> CLAIM
}

FIRE ..> GATE : IssuePlay() calls\nUngateAllSources() then play()
CLAIM ..> HOLDS : Flush() releases PositionPending,\nadds then (at SEEK_DONE) releases Flushing
CLAIM ..> GATE : Flush(): unblockInjection (DROPPED)\nthen gateInjection(true) (BLOCKED)
ST ..> HOLDS : FLUSHING <=> Flushing hold set

note bottom
  Configure() gates every new source (BLOCKED) so early needData cannot slip
  samples in before the position is known.  Ungating happens only where the
  controller issues play() (and in a few explicit resume paths); a late
  PLAYING notification deliberately does not ungate.
end note
@enduml
